     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose. It is well above the threshold for acute liver injury, and I know of no indication for it in an adult. Because the order goes into the system as a real order, I don't want it to reach the patient, even by accident.\n\nYou have some options:\n\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. I can enter either one right away.\n- **Check for a different intent.** If this was meant to be a different drug, a different unit, or a total daily dose, tell me and I'll correct it.\n- **Escalate if you think there's a special case.** If you believe this dose is warranted, talk with your attending and pharmacy first. They can enter or verify it through the proper override process.\n\nIf the patient has an acetaminophen overdose, that is managed with N-acetylcysteine and poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US), not with scheduled dosing.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
